# Scripted events for the "play" recording (natural playing: chords, slides, glissandos), in ms on the
# recording's clock. The first part transposes while chords are held, then returns to no
# transposition. The second presses a sustain pedal twice while chords are held, and the last line
# queries a setting by NRPN, sent as raw MIDI.

setting switch1 transposeUp            # the switches these events use; the others keep their defaults
setting switch2 transposeDown
setting footRight sustain

86000   press switch1                  # Transpose Up, three or more notes held (85.2-90.25 s)
86150   release switch1
97500   press switch1                  # Transpose Up again, four or more notes held (96.75-99.85 s)
97650   release switch1
215500  press switch2                  # Transpose Down, twice: back to no transposition (three or more notes held, 214.9-223.6 s)
215650  release switch2
216500  press switch2
216650  release switch2

363500  press footRight                # the sustain pedal down, four or more notes held (362.75-375.4 s)
374000  release footRight
391000  press footRight                # down with three or more notes held (390.65-394.6 s), up while four are held (399.7-401.75 s)
400500  release footRight

402000  midi B0 63 02 B0 62 2B B0 06 02 B0 26 04   # NRPN 299 = 260, query: Global MIDI CC For Foot Right Sustain
